      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Ad click aggregator system",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Ad click aggregator system",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "snPokAwjR3H1wiuvd_iU0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 278.6171875,
      "y": 207.296875,
      "width": 1089.37890625,
      "height": 1125,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1k",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2128759770,
      "version": 1373,
      "versionNonce": 1028583942,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1742641123263,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Functional requirements:\n1. User click on ads and gets redirected\n2. System tracks the number of clicks per ad\n3. Advertisers can query the system to fetch clicks based on timestamp\n\nNon functional requirements:\n1. Low latency redirection (< 500ms)\n2. Scalable (handle 10k CPS)\n3. High availability (required to maintain data integrity)\n4. Eventual consistency (system will give eventually consistent ad click data)\n5. Idempotency -> multiple ad impressions should count as one\n6. As real time as possible\n\nCore entities:\n1. Advertisement\nadId: UUID\nadvertiserId: UUID\ncampaignId: varchar(20)\ntimestamp\n\n2. AdClicks\nadClickId: UUID\nadId\nuserId\ntimestamp\n\nInput:\n1. User clicks on ad\n2. Advertiser query\n\nOutput:\n1. User gets redirected -> 302 redirect\n2. Return number of clicks per ad with granularity - 1min \n\nselect * from adclick where adId= \"123\" and timestmap >= X and timestamp <= Y\nMAX (Y - X) = 1 minute\n\nData flow:\n1. User clicks on ad\n2. User gets redirected to the website\n3. Clicks gets validated\n4. Validated clicks gets logged into DB/stream\n5. Clicks are aggregated based on ads\n6. Advertiser queries the aggregated data\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Functional requirements:\n1. User click on ads and gets redirected\n2. System tracks the number of clicks per ad\n3. Advertisers can query the system to fetch clicks based on timestamp\n\nNon functional requirements:\n1. Low latency redirection (< 500ms)\n2. Scalable (handle 10k CPS)\n3. High availability (required to maintain data integrity)\n4. Eventual consistency (system will give eventually consistent ad click data)\n5. Idempotency -> multiple ad impressions should count as one\n6. As real time as possible\n\nCore entities:\n1. Advertisement\nadId: UUID\nadvertiserId: UUID\ncampaignId: varchar(20)\ntimestamp\n\n2. AdClicks\nadClickId: UUID\nadId\nuserId\ntimestamp\n\nInput:\n1. User clicks on ad\n2. Advertiser query\n\nOutput:\n1. User gets redirected -> 302 redirect\n2. Return number of clicks per ad with granularity - 1min \n\nselect * from adclick where adId= \"123\" and timestmap >= X and timestamp <= Y\nMAX (Y - X) = 1 minute\n\nData flow:\n1. User clicks on ad\n2. User gets redirected to the website\n3. Clicks gets validated\n4. Validated clicks gets logged into DB/stream\n5. Clicks are aggregated based on ads\n6. Advertiser queries the aggregated data\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
